    "ref": "Ex 2.5 Q2(i)",
    "solution": "\\(|3x-5| = 1\\) means \\(3x-5 = 1\\) or \\(3x-5 = -1\\).\nIf \\(3x-5 = 1\\), then \\(3x = 6\\), so \\(x = 2\\).\nIf \\(3x-5 = -1\\), then \\(3x = 4\\), so \\(x = \\frac{4}{3}\\).\n\\(x = 2\\) or \\(x = \\frac{4}{3}\\)"
  },
  {
    "id": "f0ba45cb-7f2b-4e5d-baee-810a2bd67c99",
    "ref": "Ex 2.5 Q2(ii)",
    "solution": "\\(|7-2x| = 5\\) means \\(7-2x = 5\\) or \\(7-2x = -5\\).\nIf \\(7-2x = 5\\), then \\(-2x = -2\\), so \\(x = 1\\).\nIf \\(7-2x = -5\\), then \\(-2x = -12\\), so \\(x = 6\\).\n\\(x = 1\\) or \\(x = 6\\)"
  },
  {
