    "ref": "Ex 2.5 Q2(iii)",
    "solution": "\\(\\left|\\dfrac{8-x}{2}\\right| = 5\\) means \\(\\dfrac{8-x}{2} = 5\\) or \\(\\dfrac{8-x}{2} = -5\\).\nIf \\(\\dfrac{8-x}{2} = 5\\), then \\(8-x = 10\\), so \\(x = -2\\).\nIf \\(\\dfrac{8-x}{2} = -5\\), then \\(8-x = -10\\), so \\(x = 18\\).\n\\(x = -2\\) or \\(x = 18\\)"
  },
  {
