    "ref": "Ex 2.5 Q2(iv)",
    "solution": "\\(\\left|5+\\dfrac{x}{4}\\right| = 5\\) means \\(5+\\dfrac{x}{4} = 5\\) or \\(5+\\dfrac{x}{4} = -5\\).\nIf \\(5+\\dfrac{x}{4} = 5\\), then \\(\\dfrac{x}{4} = 0\\), so \\(x = 0\\).\nIf \\(5+\\dfrac{x}{4} = -5\\), then \\(\\dfrac{x}{4} = -10\\), so \\(x = -40\\).\n\\(x = 0\\) or \\(x = -40\\)"
